Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 15:59:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(v2/weather): fill null secondary fields from Open-Meteo
 with per-field attribution

- services/forecast_supplement.py: fills sunrise/sunset, UV, AQI, humidity,
  pressure, wind direction, cloud cover and sky condition ONLY where the
  selected provider left null; primary WeatherNext values are never overwritten
- /v2/weather and /weather return field_sources (weathernext | open_meteo | null)
  and a 'degraded' flag that ignores merely-unconfigured providers (IMD without
  a key is not a fallback the user should be warned about)
- hourly now starts at the current hour (no past buckets) and honours a new
  hourly_hours query param (1-168); daily rows carry weather_code, wind max,
  sunrise/sunset, uv_index_max; legacy /weather returns up to 7 days
- provenance.timezone is the IANA zone when known
- tests: 9 new offline tests incl. end-to-end fake BigQuery + fake Open-Meteo
